WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
What's up guys, my name Is Colin McNeil for theScore esports.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.679
You know, there’s a reason they call Faker
the Unkillable Demon King.

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:14.889
This guy goes beyond titles like  “series MVP” or even “world champion.” This guy

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.580
is the League of Legends G.O.A.T.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:23.680
From his incredible outplays to his surgical team
fighting skills, here are the best plays

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:26.660
from Faker's competitive League of Legends career.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:35.820
During the 2016 World Championship semifinals,
the ROX Tigers took SKT to a climactic game

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:36.830
5.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.050
While they fell behind early, Gorilla, Smeb,
and Peanut looked like they were going to

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.309
catch the star mid laner out in top lane.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:48.780
With an incredible dodge on Peanut’s cocoon
and only using his Ghost summoner spell,

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:54.220
Faker manages to get away, denying ROX the
kill on the way to his third World’s title.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:08.300
(Casting)

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.470
As one of the world's most dominant laners,
Faker often finds the slimmest openings to

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.670
solo kill his lane opponents.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.281
KT’s Nagne was trapped under the turret
by Faker’s Riven and with Wolf coming out

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:26.060
of the jungle Faker had all the support he was going to need.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.680
After a Flash to counter Nagne’s own and
an incredible sidestep to dodge the Cassiopeia

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.160
ult, Faker managed to walk out with a kill.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:42.500
(Casting)

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.780
After getting caught by the cocoon from KT’s
Score and getting dropped to less than a quarter

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:54.430
health, Faker landed a defensive ultimate
to push out Hachani’s Alistar.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:58.740
After turning back onto Score, Faker used
his Zhonya’s Hourglass to give his team

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.630
time to enter the fight.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:05.000
With a numbers advantage, Faker and SKT managed
to turn the tide.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:17.080
(Casting)

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.100
In another match against Korean rivals KT Rolster, the

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:27.270
two teams were locked in a back-and-forth teamfight in the Baron side river.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:31.050
That is, until Faker blew the fight wide open.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.409
Catching an already weak Nagne and Arrow
with his Syndra ultimate, Faker landed his E

00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:41.000
and Q on both players, killing Nagne before
finishing off Arrow with an auto attack.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:56.200
(Casting)

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:04.499
At the 2014 All-Star Paris tournament, SKT
found themselves up against Fnatic.

00:03:04.499 --> 00:03:09.239
With two players down for SKT, Fnatic decided
it was time to push Baron.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:13.819
Faker dove into the Baron pit, managing to
find a quick kill onto the enemy jungler before

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:15.989
jumping back across the wall.

00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:20.440
With the rest of SKT there to support him,
Faker jumped back in and finished off both

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.300
the Baron and xPeke to win the fight.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:34.660
(Casting)

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:43.460
During their first Worlds 2017 group stage
match, SKT faced off against Cloud9.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.740
After a pretty passive nine minutes, Contractz
decided that it was time to put the pressure

00:03:48.749 --> 00:03:49.749
on Faker.

00:03:49.749 --> 00:03:53.880
But you just don’t do that to the Unkillable
Demon King.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.900
Landing a quick ultimate and a perfectly timed
Flash under his own tower, Faker managed to

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.300
not only get away, but find a kill on Contractz.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:22.520
(Casting)

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:30.860
With Faker’s dominant lane presence in this
2016 Summer Split matchup against CJ Entus,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.280
SKT had already taken two of the middle lane
towers.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.930
With only the inhibitor turret left, three
players attempted to hold off the siege from

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.660
SKT, but Faker had other plans.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:05:02.000
(Casting)

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:10.380
Down 12 kills to one and facing a 4v5 situation
with KT’s fresh Baron buff, Faker managed

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:16.350
to land an incredible shockwave with Oriana,
getting a triple kill and helping SKT secure

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.340
the ace.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:28.960
(Casting)

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:36.860
SKT found themselves behind the eight ball early
against EDward Gaming in their second group stage game

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.060
at Worlds 2017.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.840
With Baron and dragon about to spawn, EDG
were grouped up in the mid lane.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.660
That’s when SKT initiated an explosive teamfight.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.750
Faker landed his shockwave on four of EDG’s
players, killing Meiko.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:58.270
In the end SKT managed to kill four players and
regain control of the game for their second

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.380
group stage win.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:20.200
(Casting)

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:28.000
Our number one entry on this list is one of
the best known and most viewed plays in League

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.460
of Legends history.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:36.620
Faker’s Zed outplay against Ryu is arguably
the moment that catapulted him to international

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:37.300
fame.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:44.590
Now a lot has been said about this incredible
play over the years, so let’s let Faker’s near superhuman

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.000
reactions speak for themselves.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:07:16.480
(Casting)

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.880
Kind of humbles you to see play at that level
doesn’t it?

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:26.240
Now it's got to be said, with a player as legendary as Faker is, there were a ton of awesome plays to choose from.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.400
And if you think we missed one on our list, let us know in the comments section below.

